* aged_read.spice -- physical write -> hold -> loaded-read of the 2T gain cell (issue #94, Epic #24 item 2).
* GENERATED by gen_aged_read.py; do not edit by hand.
*
* PROPOSED/UNRATIFIED SCOPE: 27 C and 125 C, tt/ss/ff/sf/fs, VDD 1.8 V only
* (spec/operating-range-decision-PROPOSED.md). CIRCUIT BODY for `klt sim` (flat, self-contained).
* Every case is an independent parallel instance: 4 cells written through M_WR (selected row written last,
* each cell starting at the OPPOSITE of its data), held with the device models evolving SN, then read:
* precharge released, selected rwl falls, corrected latch (design/sense_latch.spice) enabled 10 ns later.
* Case name m_a<age ns>_r<selected row>_v<value>_<neighbour pattern s=same/o=opposite, ascending rows>;
* c_* are NEGATIVE CONTROLS (inadequate write: wordline high level 0.55 V < Vt).
*
* ASSUMPTIONS (labelled, none is a spec value): ideal write/wordline/bitline drivers, ideal 100 ohm precharge
* switch, ideal matched dummy reference load, VREF = VRBL - 100 mV, sense instant, 4-row column,
* C_RBL = extracted 4-row worst net (post-#244), C_SN = extracted array MINIMUM wiring C (junction/gate C
* are in the device models, drawn AD/AS/PD/PS used), global corners only, NO mismatch.

